# TIL — Day 04: Shell Scripting Basics


## 1. Why Scripting in DevOps?
- Automation — avoid repeating same manual task
- Saves time, reduces human error, repeatable

## 2. touch vs vim
- touch file       # Creates empty file only
- vim file         # Creates + opens editor to write
- mkdir file       # Creates folder — not a file

## 3. Shebang #!/bin/bash
- First line of every shell script
- #!/bin/bash = use bash to run
- #!/bin/sh = use sh
- #!/bin/ksh = use ksh
- Without it, script may run with wrong shell or fail

## 4. Difference Between Shells
- bash = Bourne Again Shell, most common, what Git Bash uses
- dash = lighter and faster, used for system boot
- ksh = Korn Shell, older version, bash is improved
- Check yours: echo $SHELL

## 5. How to Run a Shell Script
- echo "Hello"             # Print to screen
- chmod +x script.sh       # Give execute permission
- ./script.sh              # Run it
- Without chmod +x = Permission denied

## 6. CPU and RAM Check
- top                      # Live CPU and RAM usage
- lscpu			   # CPU information
- nproc 		   # Number of CPUs
- top                      # Live CPU, RAM, processes — press q to exit
- top then press M         # Sort by memory
- top then press P         # Sort by CPU
- htop                     # Better version of top (needs install)
**sudo apt install htop**  # if htop is not found you can install it with this command
- free -m                  # RAM in MB
- free -h                  # RAM in human readable
